tps://github.com/aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","login":"aaronfranke","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#pullrequestreview-3003410136","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104112","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-09T23:41:59Z"},{"id":3285318340,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7D0frE","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?u=a5fd9a203c90bd196083e33bbf0e21324e8c68f8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","login":"adamscott","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott"},"body":"As stated, I think this fix is welcome. Primarily because even if we find a better solution to the platform rounding errors, this fix stays relevant. This is because `sRGB{0,0,0} == OK_HSL{0,0,0}` is always `true`. We even prevent superfluous calculation here!\n\nIt doesn't mean though that we shouldn't think harder to fix issuers with rounding errors. I just don't think the fix goes against the idea.\n\n---\n\nSmall suggestion.\n\nI would instead edit [thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h) to add that check instead of in `Color`. Seems cleaner.\n\nHere's the `thirdparty/misc/patches/ok_color-0001-srgb_to_okhsl_precision.patch` file if you follow my suggestion:\n```diff\ndiff --git a/thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h b/thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h\nindex 4d0f0049bd..2cc7f1ceef 100644\n--- a/thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h\n+++ b/thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h\n@@ -541,6 +541,11 @@ static RGB okhsl_to_srgb(HSL hsl)\n \n static HSL srgb_to_okhsl(RGB rgb)\n {\n+\t// Fixes some precision errors.\n+\tif (rgb.r == 0.0f && rgb.g == 0.0f && rgb.b == 0.0f) {\n+\t\treturn { 0.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f };\n+\t}\n+\n \tLab lab = linear_srgb_to_oklab({\n \t\tsrgb_transfer_function_inv(rgb.r),\n \t\tsrgb_transfer_function_inv(rgb.g),\n\n```","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#pullrequestreview-3285318340","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104112","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-09-30T14:37:06Z"},{"id":3285320970,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7D0gUK","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?u=a5fd9a203c90bd196083e33bbf0e21324e8c68f8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","login":"adamscott","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott"},"body":"Sorry, it seems that I forgot to click on approve.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#pullrequestreview-3285320970","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104112","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-09-30T14:37:34Z"},{"id":3285489018,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7D1JV6","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"52fec34cab269f1497d25299716d4822d127b4f1","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?u=24618295fece29a0bf5c850faf2555985232f5f2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","login":"aaronfranke","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#pullrequestreview-3285489018","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104112","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-09-30T15:06:43Z"},{"id":3423110646,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7MCIX2","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"52fec34cab269f1497d25299716d4822d127b4f1","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Discussed at the core meeting.\r\n\r\nFor this case, this is a good solution since it's simple and may also bring more expected results to users of the function.\r\n\r\nFor future problems like this, we should consider using explicit defaults. The problem probably cannot be solved 'in general' since we expect float inconsistencies to happen every now and then, and checking nearness in docs or using deterministic calculations are probably overkill for this problem.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104112#pullrequestreview-3423110646","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104112","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-11-05T16:19:54Z"}]